# Operator manuals in AIC Server (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-19), verbatim intent:

> **All of the workstation assurance, agents, configuration programs,
> installers all require manuals for their operation that should include
> graphics and screen shots. The manuals should be included in the AIC
> Server. All manuals should have an export to PDF option as well as be
> localized.**

## The rule

> **Every operator-facing component — Workstation Assurance, agents,
> configurators, elevate helpers, launchers, and installers — ships an
> operation manual that lives in AIC Server (reachable in-product), includes
> current graphics and screenshots with meaningful alt text, offers PDF
> export, and is localized per Tier 1 language catalogs. Loose files beside
> the product are not delivery. A chapter that describes unimplemented
> behavior is forbidden.**

## Governing register (explicit)

These are **operator / administrator manuals**. Localization quality and
register follow [`enterprise-localization.mdc`](enterprise-localization.mdc)
and the must-localize / installer catalog rules in
[`compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc`](compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc)
and [`multilingual-tier-1-installer.mdc`](multilingual-tier-1-installer.mdc).

The sixth-grade plain-language bar in
[`training-materials-plain-language-and-images.mdc`](training-materials-plain-language-and-images.mdc)
governs **workforce training and welcome letters**, not operator manuals.
Do **not** rewrite operator manuals to grade 6. The **image-rich**
requirement here is parallel to that training rule’s illustration
requirement, but it is a separate obligation for operator documentation.

## When it applies

Trigger phrases (non-exhaustive): operator manual, product manuals,
configurator / elevate / installer / WA / agent documentation for
operators, “manuals in the server,” PDF export for manuals, screenshot
runbooks.

Does **not** force a full manual rewrite for a narrowly scoped chrome
fix that explicitly scopes out documentation (still must not claim
manuals are complete). Internal `docs/dev` engineer runbooks are not a
substitute for in-product operator manuals.

## Required

1. **Coverage** — One operation manual (or named chapter set under
   Documentation) for each family: Workstation Assurance; endpoint /
   recording / Jump / DB / related **agents**; **configuration programs**
   (server, agent, Jump, DB, WA, recording configurators); **elevate
   helpers**; **product launchers**; **installers / MSI deployment**.
2. **In AIC Server** — Manuals are reachable from the admin SPA
   Documentation (or equivalent in-product surface). Shipping only a repo
   Markdown file, a README next to an MSI, or a PDF on a share is **not**
   delivery.
3. **Graphics and screenshots** — Required, not optional. At least one
   current screenshot or original diagram per major procedure. Screenshots
   must carry load-bearing alt text (Section 508 / WCAG 1.1.1) and captions
   that teach the step. Images must survive PDF export (embedded in the
   export package, not browser-only decoration).
4. **Image provenance** — Original captures from a clean demo state, or
   original / public-domain / permissively licensed art with license
   recorded. Branding marks from `core-assets` only
   ([`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc)). Never third-party
   copyrighted screenshots or stock art under unclear licenses.
5. **No lab leaks in images or captions** — No lab hostnames, lab account
   names, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit wiring, agent commentary, or other
   internal lab configuration
   ([`no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc`](no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc)).
   Capture from a clean demo / product-language state.
6. **PDF export** — Every manual offers an operator-visible export to PDF
   (server-rendered when available; honest refusal + documented fallback
   only when the engine is not compiled — never silent format substitution).
7. **Localized** — English source plus catalogs for every required Tier 1
   tag; catalogs ship with the installer. New or changed English manual
   source enqueues a localization-work item in the same change set
   ([`localization-work-queue.mdc`](localization-work-queue.mdc)).
8. **Honesty** — Describe what ships today. Do not document unimplemented
   behavior as live ([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc)).
9. **Support-program Tier 1 honesty** — When the underlying support
   program UI is only Partial multilingual (see
   `core-assets/docs/dev/support-programs-multilingual-audit-20260819.md`),
   manuals for that program must not claim Tier 1 localization ahead of
   the software. Report **Partial** / **BLOCKED** honestly.

## Forbidden

- Claiming manuals “done” because engineer `docs/dev` or crate READMEs exist
- Operator manuals only as loose files beside an MSI or Desktop shortcut
- Text-only chapters with no graphics/screenshots when the surface is GUI
- Screenshots without alt text, or screenshots that leak lab configuration
- Third-party copyrighted images or reworded competitor manuals
- Advertising PDF export when the server cannot deliver PDF bytes (false
  green) — gate on engine availability like Assessment Binder
- Shipping English-only operator manuals when other Tier 1 packs already
  ship for Documentation
- Closing localization-work with agent-draft catalogs only
- Applying the workforce grade-6 training rule as the operator-manual
  reading-level bar
- Describing unimplemented features as available in a manual

## Worked violation to fix

**Violation.** Agent and WA MSIs ship; operators get a README on the
install share. Admin Manuals under `/docs/admin` mention “Agent
Configuration” in prose with no screenshots, no PDF button, and no WA
or installer chapters. Support-program UIs are Partial multilingual, but
a status note claims “all manuals Tier 1 complete.”

**Fix.** Author in-product manuals under Documentation (extend the
existing manual chapter model or a dedicated family section), embed
current demo-state screenshots with alt text, wire PDF export through
the existing binder PDF seam (or an honest Print/PDF path until the
engine is on), enqueue localization-work for new English source, stage
locale catalogs in the Server installer, and keep status Partial for any
family whose UI is not yet Tier 1.

